"An Avowed's Foundation has two parts: Foundational Enhancements and Class Effects."
"One point is roughly a 10 percent improvement over the species average."
"Rank-based class stat bonuses are standard for every class and rank except uniques."
"Points count up from zero, not from the person's own base stats."
"Each top-level stat splits across sub-stats; Appeal runs from facial symmetry to empathy."
"Under the 1963 Agreement the psychological share of a stat can be deleted before affixing."
"Deleting it is seen as a bad look for heroes."
"Stats include Appeal, Agility, Speed, Reflexes, Instinct, Balance, Stamina and Dexterity."
"Too much Instinct can make a person paranoid."
"The System hard-limits organic thinking power for almost everyone."
"An extra half point of mental processing takes about six months to affix gradually."
"Top Avowed get their thinking supplemented with magical effects instead."
"Skills add foundational supplements; about ten in total is normal."
"S-ranks get extra free points to place."
"The System generalizes Appeal unless the Avowed makes special requests."
